{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nCopyright (c) 2025 Oliver Butterley. All rights reserved.\nReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\nAuthors: Oliver Butterley, Yoh Tanimoto\n-/\n\n\n\nimport Mathlib\nimport Mathlib.MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Basic\nimport Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Group.Basic\n\n/-!\n# Integral with respect to a complex-valued measure\n\nThree options come to mind for defining the integral with respect to a complex-valued measure:\n\n1. Define the integral with respect to a complex measure by decomposing the measure into real and imaginary parts and then using the definition of integral with respect to a signed measure. I.e.,\n```\nnoncomputable def integral (μ : SignedMeasure α) (f : α → G) : G :=\n    ∫ a, f a ∂μ.toJordanDecomposition.posPart - ∫ a, f a ∂μ.toJordanDecomposition.negPart\n```\nIn turn, the integral with respect to as signed measure is defined using the Jordan decomposition\ninto positive and negative parts.\n\n2. Develop directly the integral with respect to any `VectorMeasure` by introducing simple\nfunctions, etc.\n\n3. Use the polar decomposition of a complex measure into total variation measure and angular\nfunction and hence use the definition of a Bochner integral.\n\nIt is unclear what the best design choice is so at the moment we opt for using polar decomposition\nas the definition.\n\nWhatever the direction taken with these definitions, the different components should be separated\ninto their own files.\n\n## Main definitions\n\n* `ComplexMeasure.integral`\n\n## Notation\n\n* `∫ a, f a ∂μ` : integral of `f` with respect to a `ComplexMeasure` `μ`\n\n## To do\n\n* Add many other relevant results.\n\n-/\n\n@[expose] public section\n\nnamespace MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure\n\nopen MeasureTheory\n\nvariable {α : Type*} [MeasurableSpace α]\nvariable {G : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℂ G]\n\n/-! ## Polar decomposition of complex measures. -/\n\nlemma variation_neg_complex (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).variation = μ.variation := by\n  unfold VectorMeasure.variation\n  simp\n\n/-- The variation measure part in the polar decomposition of a complex measure. -/\nnoncomputable def var (μ : ComplexMeasure α) := μ.variation\n\n@[simp]\nlemma var_neg (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).var = μ.var := by\n  simp [var, variation_neg_complex]\n\n/-- The angular part (density function) in the polar decomposition of a complex measure. -/\nnoncomputable def ang (μ : ComplexMeasure α) := μ.rnDeriv μ.var\n\n@[simp]\nlemma ang_neg (μ : ComplexMeasure α) : (-μ).ang = -μ.ang := by\n  -- To do: adjust this statement to the `μ`-a.e. version.\n  sorry\n\n/-! ## Definition of the integral. -/\n\n/-- Change of variables for the integral with respect to a complex measure defined by a density. -/\nlemma integral_withDensityᵥ_eq (μ : Measure α) [SigmaFinite μ] (h : α → ℂ)\n    (hf : Integrable h μ) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (μ.withDensityᵥ h).integral f = ∫ x, h x • f x ∂μ := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  -- We need to show that (μ.withDensityᵥ h).var and (μ.withDensityᵥ h).ang\n  -- are related to |h| and h/|h|.\n  sorry\n\nnotation3 \"∫ \"(...)\", \"r:60:(scoped f => f)\" ∂\"μ:70 => integral μ r\n\n/-! ## Some lemmas related to the integral. -/\n\n/-- For complex measures `μ`, `ν` and integrable function `f`: `∫ f d(μ + ν) = ∫ f dμ + ∫ f dν` -/\nlemma integral_add (μ ν : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (μ + ν).integral f = μ.integral f + ν.integral f := by\n  let λ := μ.variation + ν.variation\n  have : IsFiniteMeasure λ := inferInstance\n  have hμλ : μ ≪ᵥ λ.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    apply VectorMeasure.AbsolutelyContinuous.mk\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have : ‖μ s‖ₑ ≤ μ.variation s := by\n      rw [VectorMeasure.variation, VectorMeasure.ennrealToMeasure_apply hmeas]\n      exact MeasureTheory.preVariation.sum_le (‖μ ·‖ₑ) hmeas (Finpartition.top hmeas)\n    have : μ s = 0 := by\n      have : ‖μ s‖ₑ = 0 := by \n        apply le_antisymm _ (by positivity)\n        calc ‖μ s‖ₑ ≤ μ.variation s := this\n          _ ≤ λ s := Measure.le_iff.mp (Measure.le_add_right (le_refl _)) s\n          _ = 0 := hs\n      exact enorm_eq_zero.mp this\n    exact this\n  have hνλ : ν ≪ᵥ λ.toENNRealVectorMeasure := by\n    apply VectorMeasure.AbsolutelyContinuous.mk\n    intro s hmeas hs\n    rw [Measure.toENNRealVectorMeasure_apply_measurable hmeas] at hs\n    have : ‖ν s‖ₑ ≤ ν.variation s := by\n      rw [VectorMeasure.variation, VectorMeasure.ennrealToMeasure_apply hmeas]\n      exact MeasureTheory.preVariation.sum_le (‖ν ·‖ₑ) hmeas (Finpartition.top hmeas)\n    have : ν s = 0 := by\n      have : ‖ν s‖ₑ = 0 := by \n        apply le_antisymm _ (by positivity)\n        calc ‖ν s‖ₑ ≤ ν.variation s := this\n          _ ≤ λ s := Measure.le_iff.mp (Measure.le_add_left (le_refl _)) s\n          _ = 0 := hs\n      exact enorm_eq_zero.mp this\n    exact this\n  obtain ⟨hμ, hμ_int, hμ_eq⟩ := exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation_λ μ λ hμλ\n  obtain ⟨hν, hν_int, hν_eq⟩ := exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation_λ ν λ hνλ\n  rw [hμ_eq, hν_eq, ← Measure.withDensityᵥ_add hμ_int hν_int]\n  rw [integral_withDensityᵥ_eq λ (hμ + hν) (hμ_int.add hν_int) f]\n  rw [integral_withDensityᵥ_eq λ hμ hμ_int f]\n  rw [integral_withDensityᵥ_eq λ hν hν_int f]\n  simp only [Pi.add_apply, smul_add]\n  rw [MeasureTheory.integral_add]\n  · exact (hμ_int.smul f).integrableOn -- assuming f is bounded\n  · exact (hν_int.smul f).integrableOn\n\nlemma integral_neg (μ  : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (-μ).integral f = -μ.integral f := by\n  simp [integral, MeasureTheory.integral_neg]\n\nlemma integral_sub (μ₁ μ₂  : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (μ₁ - μ₂).integral f = μ₁.integral f - μ₂.integral f := by\n  calc\n    _ = (μ₁ + (-μ₂)).integral f := by rfl\n    _ = μ₁.integral f + (-μ₂).integral f := by exact integral_add μ₁ (-μ₂) _\n    _ = _ := by rw [integral_neg, sub_eq_add_neg]\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the measure: `∫ f d(c • μ) = c • ∫ f dμ` -/\nlemma integral_smul_measure (c : ℂ) (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    (c • μ).integral f = c • μ.integral f := by\n  -- Proof outline: similar to `integral_add`, use RN density with respect to a dominating measure.\n  sorry\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the function: `∫ (c • f) dμ = c • ∫ f dμ` -/\nlemma integral_const_smul (c : ℂ) (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) :\n    μ.integral (fun a => c • f a) = c • μ.integral f := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  simp_rw [smul_comm]\n  rw [MeasureTheory.integral_smul]\n\n/-- The integral is linear with respect to the function: `∫ (f + g) dμ = ∫ f dμ + ∫ g dμ` -/\nlemma integral_add_function (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f g : α → ℂ) :\n    μ.integral (fun a => f a + g a) = μ.integral f + μ.integral g := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  simp_rw [smul_add]\n  rw [MeasureTheory.integral_add]\n  · exact (Integrable.smul μ.ang (sorry : Integrable f μ.var)).integrableOn\n  · exact (Integrable.smul μ.ang (sorry : Integrable g μ.var)).integrableOn\n\n/-- The integral of `f` against `μ` is bounded by `variation μ * ‖f‖_∞`. -/\nlemma integral_bound_of_variation_le (μ : ComplexMeasure α) (f : α → ℂ) (C : ℝ)\n    (hf : ∀ x, ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖μ.integral f‖ ≤ (μ.variation Set.univ).toReal * C := by\n  dsimp [integral]\n  calc\n    ‖MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun x => μ.ang x • f x)‖\n        ≤ MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun x => ‖μ.ang x • f x‖) := norm_integral_le_integral_norm _\n    _ ≤ MeasureTheory.integral μ.var (fun _ => C) := by\n        apply MeasureTheory.integral_mono\n        · -- integrable ‖μ.ang x • f x‖\n          sorry\n        · -- integrable C\n          sorry\n        · intro x\n          rw [norm_smul]\n          -- need ‖μ.ang x‖ ≤ 1\n          sorry\n    _ = (μ.variation Set.univ).toReal * C := by\n        rw [MeasureTheory.integral_const]\n        simp [var]\n\nend MeasureTheory.ComplexMeasure\n","mtime":1778536367717}